    "narrative": "Ghost Ride the WHIP enters June 2nd with a focus on exploiting exploitable arms, headlined by **Corbin Carroll** (77.40) and **Jose Caballero** (70.71). Both benefit from high-leverage matchups against Eric Lauer and Joey Cantillo, respectively; **Carroll**\u2019s elite speed profile against a lefty allows him to maximize his efficiency, while **Caballero**\u2019s 13% platoon boost makes him an essential play despite hitting out of the 8-hole. **Tyler Soderstrom** (65.10) also emerges as a strong play against Jameson Taillon, with the positive park factors and SP skill rating outweighing a marginal wind-in concern. Conversely, **Brice Turang** (47.50) faces a difficult task against Trevor McDonald; while his speed is a critical asset, the combination of a sub-3.00 xERA and a minor penalty from an elite catcher\u2019s pop time forces a more tempered outlook today.\n\nThe decision to bench **Kyle Karros** (48.57) was the tightest call on the board. While **Karros** posted a competitive score against Grayson Rodriguez\u2014bolstered by the pitcher's elevated xERA\u2014he was ultimately squeezed out by the batting order efficiency of players like **Zach McKinstry** and **Travis Bazzana**. **Bazzana**\u2019s leadoff spot provides a +10% boost that ultimately created the separation needed to keep him in the utility mix. We are monitoring \"Lineup Pending\" statuses closely, particularly for **Dalton Rushing** and **Josh Naylor**; **Rushing** specifically faces a risk of regression if he remains buried in the 8-hole against Michael Soroka. Owners should also watch the wind reports, as the inward breeze significantly drags down the daily efficiency for **Austin Riley** and **Seiya Suzuki**, capping their ceiling despite favorable individual matchups.",
